Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

core/logging_config.py is the single source of truth for how JQE
logs: console + rotating file sinks, format, level, rotation and
retention policy — all driven by config.settings so they're
configurable via environment variables without touching code.
configure_logging() is idempotent, so importing it from multiple
modules never duplicates sinks or log lines.

core/logger.py becomes a thin backward-compatible shim re-exporting
the same logger object, since five existing modules already import
'from core.logger import logger'. This keeps the change to a single
internal implementation swap rather than five call-site edits.
